or a family member to start tracking medicines.",create_profile_btn:"Create Profile",create_my_profile_btn:"Create My Profile",default_family_name:"My Family",view_prescriptions_btn:"Prescriptions & Documents",documents_sub:"Upload prescriptions, lab reports, and other medical documents",sheet_title_choose_who:"Who Is This For?",sheet_title_profile_details:"Profile Details",choose_who_helper:"Pick a family member, or choose \"Someone Else\" if they don't have an account or aren't in your family yet.",dependent_badge:"Dependent",other_option_title:"Someone Else",other_option_sub:"No account, or not added to your family yet",back_btn:"\u2039 Back",for_member_label:"For {{name}}",label_full_name:"Full Name",placeholder_person_name:"e.g. Grandma Sharma",label_category:"Category",category_self:"Myself",category_kid:"Child",category_elder:"Elder",label_dob:"Date of Birth",placeholder_dob:"Tap to select a date",prescriptions_header_title:"Prescriptions",upload_document_btn:"Upload Document",upload_document_sub:"Photo, PDF, or Word file",documents_empty:"No documents uploaded yet.",ocr_status_label:"Status",prescription_failed_title:"Couldn't Read Prescription",prescription_failed_msg:"We couldn't read that document \u2014 it may be blurry or in an unsupported format. You can still add medicines manually.",prescription_processed_title:"Prescription Processed",prescription_processed_msg:"Your prescription was uploaded. Whichever medicines could be read from it have been added to your list.",prescription_empty_msg:"Your prescription was uploaded, but we couldn't find any medicines in it.",confirm_quantity_invalid_msg:"Please enter a valid quantity.",ocr_status_pending:"Reading\u2026",ocr_status_processed:"Processed",ocr_status_failed:"Couldn't read",confirm_quantity_title:"Confirm Quantity",confirm_quantity_progress:"{{current}} of {{total}}",confirm_quantity_intro:"We added {{name}} from your prescription. How much do you have?",confirm_quantity_save:"Save & Continue",confirm_quantity_skip:"Skip for now",error_generic:"Something went wrong. Please try again.",error_not_found:"That medicine or profile no longer exists.",error_no_permission:"You don't have permission to do that.",category_other:"Other",choose_camera:"Camera",choose_gallery:"Gallery",choose_document:"PDF / Word Document",view_fullscreen:"View Fullscreen",delete_document:"Delete Document",delete_doc_confirm_title:"Delete Document",delete_doc_confirm_msg:"Are you sure you want to delete this document?"},wellness:{header_title:"Mind & Mood",add_btn:"Log",hero_title:"How you have been feeling",hero_subtitle:"Check in whenever the mood shifts. Everything here stays on this device.",stat_today:"Check-ins today",stat_average:"7-day average",stat_streak:"Day streak",checkin_title:"Check in right now",checkin_sub:"Tap the face that fits this moment",mood_1:"Very low",mood_2:"Low",mood_3:"Okay",mood_4:"Good",mood_5:"Great",factor_work:"Work",factor_family:"Family",factor_sleep:"Sleep",factor_health:"Health",factor_money:"Money",factor_self:"Myself",trend_title:"Last 7 days",trend_meta:"Average per day",trend_oldest:"7 days ago",trend_today:"Today",trend_factors:"Most mentioned lately",cbt_title:"CBT assistant",cbt_sub:"A short, guided exercise based on your last check-in",cbt_idle_title:"Want to talk it through?",cbt_idle_sub:"I will pick an exercise that matches how you last felt.",cbt_idle_no_entry:"Log a mood first, and I will suggest an exercise that fits it.",cbt_start:"Talk it through",cbt_again:"Suggest another exercise",cbt_pick_label:"Or choose a technique yourself",cbt_disclaimer:"These exercises are self-help guidance, not medical advice. If you are in distress or thinking about harming yourself, please contact a local health professional or emergency service.",cbt_tone_low:"That sounds heavy, and it makes sense that it is hard right now. Let us take one small step together rather than fixing everything at once.",cbt_tone_mixed:"It sounds like a mixed stretch \u2014 some of it fine, some of it not. That is worth taking seriously either way.",cbt_tone_steady:"A steady day is a real result, not a nothing day. Let us keep a little of that steadiness for tomorrow.",cbt_tone_bright:"Good to hear things feel lighter. Noticing what helped is what makes it repeatable.",cbt_reframe_title:"Reframe the thought",cbt_reframe_step_1:"Write down the exact thought that keeps returning, in the words you actually use.",cbt_reframe_step_2:"List one piece of evidence for it and one against it. Just one each is enough.",cbt_reframe_step_3:"Rewrite the thought so it stays true but fits both pieces of evidence.",cbt_reframe_prompt:"If a friend said this thought out loud, what would you answer them?",cbt_grounding_title:"Ground yourself",cbt_grounding_step_1:"Put both feet flat on the floor and notice the weight of your body on the chair.",cbt_grounding_step_2:"Name five things you can see, four you can hear, and three you can touch.",cbt_grounding_step_3:"Say the date and where you are, out loud or silently.",cbt_grounding_prompt:"What is one thing in this room that is genuinely safe right now?",cbt_breathing_title:"Slow the breath",cbt_breathing_step_1:"Breathe in through your nose for a count of four.",cbt_breathing_step_2:"Hold gently for four, then breathe out for six.",cbt_breathing_step_3:"Repeat six times, letting the out-breath stay longer than the in-breath.",cbt_breathing_prompt:"What is different in your shoulders and jaw now compared with a minute ago?",cbt_gratitude_title:"Notice what held",cbt_gratitude_step_1:"Name one thing today that went the way you hoped, however small.",cbt_gratitude_step_2:"Name one person who made the day easier, and how.",cbt_gratitude_step_3:"Name one thing you did yourself that you would not want overlooked.",cbt_gratitude_prompt:"Which of those three is worth carrying into tomorrow?",med_title:"Guided meditations",med_sub:"Structured sessions you can follow without sound or a connection",med_minutes:"{{count}} min",med_note:"Move at your own pace. Stopping early is fine \u2014 a short session you finish is worth more than a long one you dread.",med_done:"Done",med_cat_breath:"Breath",med_cat_calm:"Calm",med_cat_sleep:"Sleep",med_cat_focus:"Focus",med_box_breath_title:"Box breathing",med_box_breath_sub:"An even, four-count rhythm for when the body is running faster than the situation needs.",med_box_breath_step_1:"Sit upright, rest your hands, and let your eyes close or soften.",med_box_breath_step_2:"Breathe in for four counts, hold for four.",med_box_breath_step_3:"Breathe out for four counts, hold empty for four.",med_box_breath_step_4:"Continue for sixteen rounds, then sit still for a moment before moving.",med_body_scan_title:"Body scan",med_body_scan_sub:"A slow pass from head to feet, releasing what has quietly tightened during the day.",med_body_scan_step_1:"Lie down or sit back, and take three unhurried breaths.",med_body_scan_step_2:"Bring attention to your scalp, face and jaw, and let each soften as you exhale.",med_body_scan_step_3:"Move down through shoulders, arms, chest, stomach, hips and legs, pausing at each.",med_body_scan_step_4:"Finish at your feet, then notice the whole body at once for a final minute.",med_wind_down_title:"Evening wind-down",med_wind_down_sub:"A ten-minute close to the day, for a mind that keeps working after the lights go off.",med_wind_down_step_1:"Put the phone face down and dim the light in the room.",med_wind_down_step_2:"Breathe out slowly five times, longer out than in.",med_wind_down_step_3:"Name three things from today you are setting down until tomorrow.",med_wind_down_step_4:"Rest attention on the weight of the blanket or the sound of the room, and let it stay there.",med_focus_reset_title:"Three-minute reset",med_focus_reset_sub:"A short reset between tasks, for when attention has scattered but the day is not over.",med_focus_reset_step_1:"Stop what you are doing and sit back from the screen.",med_focus_reset_step_2:"For one minute, notice what you are feeling without changing it.",med_focus_reset_step_3:"For one minute, follow the breath in and out.",med_focus_reset_step_4:"For one minute, widen attention to the whole body, then choose the one next thing.",history_title:"Your check-ins",history_sub:"Tap an entry to edit or remove it",empty_title:"No check-ins yet",empty_sub:"Log how you feel once, and the trend and coaching will start working from it.",sheet_title_add:"Log your mood",sheet_title_edit:"Edit check-in",label_mood:"How do you feel?",label_factors:"What is behind it?",label_note:"Anything you want to add",placeholder_note:"Optional \u2014 a sentence is plenty",save_entry:"Save check-in",save_changes:"Save changes",delete_entry:"Delete this check-in",delete_confirm_title:"Delete check-in",delete_confirm_msg:"This check-in will be removed from your history and from the 7-day trend.",cancel:"Cancel",delete:"Delete",privacy_note:"Mood entries are stored only on this device. They are not shared with your family group and are never uploaded.",offline_banner:"Showing your saved copy \u2014 we couldn't reach the server.",sync_failed_title:"Couldn't save",sync_failed_msg:"We couldn't reach the server. Check your connection and try again.",load_more:"Load more",uplift_title:"A lift for today",uplift_activity:"Try this",uplift_affirmation:"Say to yourself",reco_title:"Suggested for you",reco_based_on:"Because today felt {{mood}}",chat_title:"Talk it through",chat_sub:"Tell the assistant what's on your mind. It replies with a CBT technique to try.",chat_empty:"Nothing here yet. Say what today has been like and the assistant takes it from there.",chat_placeholder:"What's on your mind?",chat_send:"Send message",chat_offline_note:"The assistant is unreachable right now, so this reply came from the offline coach on your device.",chat_clear_title:"Clear this conversation?",chat_clear_msg:"Every message in this chat will be deleted. This cannot be undone.",ex_title:"Exercises",ex_sub:"Short, guided practices. Mark one done and it counts towards your streak.",ex_cat_all:"All",ex_cat_cbt_technique:"CBT",ex_cat_breath:"Breath",ex_cat_sleep:"Sleep",ex_cat_focus:"Focus",ex_cat_mindfulness:"Mindfulness",ex_complete:"I finished this",ex_done_title:"Session logged",ex_done_msg:"{{title}} is saved to your wellness history.",ex_empty_title:"No exercises here",ex_empty_sub:"Try another category, or pull down to refresh.",label_reason:"Reason",placeholder_reason:"In a few words, what brought this on?"},cycle:{header_title:"Cycle & Life Stage",add_btn:"Log",hero_no_data_title:"Start tracking",hero_no_data_sub:"Log one period and predictions begin from there",hero_day:"Day {{day}} of your cycle",progress_caption:"Day {{day}} of about {{length}}",stat_days_to_period:"Days to period",stat_late:"Days late",late_by:"{{days}}",stat_cycle_length:"Cycle length",stat_logged:"Periods logged",phase_menstrual:"Menstrual phase",phase_follicular:"Follicular phase",phase_ovulation:"Ovulation window",phase_luteal:"Luteal phase",stage_title:"Life stage",stage_sub:"This changes what is predicted and which guidance is shown",stage_cycling_name:"Tracking",stage_cycling_desc:"Ordinary cycle tracking, with predictions for your next period, ovulation and fertile window.",stage_cycling_nutrition_1:"Keep iron up around your period \u2014 lentils, dark greens, and meat or fish if you eat them.",stage_cycling_nutrition_2:"Pair iron-rich food with vitamin C, such as lemon or amla, to absorb more of it.",stage_cycling_nutrition_3:"Steady the luteal-phase energy dip with complex carbohydrates rather than quick sugar.",stage_cycling_exercise_1:"Keep heavier training for the week after your period, when energy usually peaks.",stage_cycling_exercise_2:"Swap intensity for walking, yoga or stretching on the heaviest days.",stage_cycling_exercise_3:"Track how each phase feels for two cycles before changing your routine.",stage_fertility_name:"Fertility",stage_fertility_desc:"Planning for pregnancy. The fertile window and ovulation estimate are highlighted, with a reminder before the window opens.",stage_fertility_nutrition_1:"Take folate daily, ideally from before conception, on medical advice.",stage_fertility_nutrition_2:"Include whole grains, pulses and healthy fats; keep alcohol and heavy caffeine low.",stage_fertility_nutrition_3:"Ask a doctor about vitamin D and B12 rather than guessing at supplements.",stage_fertility_exercise_1:"Moderate activity most days supports fertility better than long, intense sessions.",stage_fertility_exercise_2:"Strength work twice a week helps insulin sensitivity, which matters for ovulation.",stage_fertility_exercise_3:"Protect sleep and manage stress \u2014 both affect cycles as much as training does.",stage_postpartum_name:"Postpartum",stage_postpartum_desc:"Recovery after birth. Cycles often return late and irregularly, especially while breastfeeding, so predictions stay deliberately cautious.",stage_postpartum_nutrition_1:"Eat regularly and drink more than usual, particularly if you are breastfeeding.",stage_postpartum_nutrition_2:"Keep protein, iron and calcium up while your body rebuilds its stores.",stage_postpartum_nutrition_3:"Continue any prescribed supplements until your doctor says otherwise.",stage_postpartum_exercise_1:"Start with walking and breathing work, and get clearance before anything heavier.",stage_postpartum_exercise_2:"Rebuild the pelvic floor and deep abdominal muscles before returning to impact.",stage_postpartum_exercise_3:"Stop and ask for advice if you notice leaking, pain or a gap along the midline.",stage_perimenopause_name:"Perimenopause",stage_perimenopause_desc:"The years before periods stop, when cycles get shorter, longer or skip entirely. Predictions here are indicative only.",stage_perimenopause_nutrition_1:"Prioritise calcium and vitamin D \u2014 bone loss speeds up in this stage.",stage_perimenopause_nutrition_2:"Keep protein at every meal to hold on to muscle.",stage_perimenopause_nutrition_3:"Notice whether caffeine, alcohol or spice trigger hot flushes for you, and adjust.",stage_perimenopause_exercise_1:"Strength training twice a week protects bone density and muscle.",stage_perimenopause_exercise_2:"Add weight-bearing movement such as brisk walking or stair climbing.",stage_perimenopause_exercise_3:"Balance work now reduces fall risk considerably later.",stage_menopause_name:"Menopause",stage_menopause_desc:"Twelve months or more without a period. Cycle prediction is switched off, and the focus moves to symptoms, bone health and long-term wellbeing.",stage_menopause_nutrition_1:"Keep calcium and vitamin D consistent, and have levels checked periodically.",stage_menopause_nutrition_2:"Fibre and healthy fats support heart health, which needs more attention after menopause.",stage_menopause_nutrition_3:"Watch portion drift rather than dieting \u2014 metabolism shifts gradually, not overnight.",stage_menopause_exercise_1:"Keep strength training twice a week; it is the single most protective habit here.",stage_menopause_exercise_2:"Aim for regular moderate cardio for heart and mood.",stage_menopause_exercise_3:"Yoga or stretching helps with stiffness and sleep quality.",prediction_title:"What comes next",prediction_sub:"Estimated from the periods you have logged",next_period:"Next period expected",ovulation:"Estimated ovulation",fertile_window:"Fertile window",confidence_low:"Low confidence",confidence_medium:"Fair confidence",confidence_high:"Good confidence",confidence_note:"Based on {{count}} completed cycles",prediction_disclaimer:"These are estimates from your own logged dates, not a medical assessment, and they are not reliable as contraception.",prediction_empty_title:"Nothing to predict yet",prediction_empty_sub:"Log the first day of your last period and an estimate appears immediately, sharpening with each cycle you add.",prediction_menopause_title:"Prediction is off",prediction_menopause_sub:"You have set your life stage to menopause, so no next period is predicted. Symptom logging and guidance stay available.",reminders_title:"Reminders",reminders_sub:"What you would be alerted about, based on today",reminders_toggle:"Cycle reminders",reminders_pending_note:"Shown inside the app for now. Phone notifications arrive once the app's reminder system is added.",reminders_empty:"Nothing coming up in the next few days.",reminder_period_soon:"Period expected soon",reminder_fertile_window:"Fertile window opens",reminder_period_late:"Period is later than expected",reminder_log_open_period:"Add an end date to your current period",reminder_in_days:"in {{count}} days",guidance_title:"Guidance for you",guidance_sub:"Tailored to your stage: {{stage}}",guidance_nutrition:"Nutrition",guidance_exercise:"Movement",history_title:"Logged periods",history_sub:"Tap an entry to edit or remove it",empty_title:"No periods logged yet",empty_sub:"Add the first day of your most recent period to begin.",entry_ongoing:"Still ongoing \u2014 add an end date when it finishes",flow_light:"Light",flow_medium:"Medium",flow_heavy:"Heavy",symptom_cramps:"Cramps",symptom_headache:"Headache",symptom_fatigue:"Fatigue",symptom_bloating:"Bloating",symptom_mood_swings:"Mood swings",symptom_tender_breasts:"Tender breasts",symptom_acne:"Acne",symptom_insomnia:"Poor sleep",sheet_title_add:"Log a period",sheet_title_edit:"Edit period",label_start:"First day",label_end:"Last day",label_flow:"Flow",label_symptoms:"Symptoms",label_note:"Notes",placeholder_date:"YYYY-MM-DD",placeholder_end:"Leave empty if it is still ongoing",placeholder_note:"Optional",end_hint:"Use the \u2212 and + buttons to move a day at a time, or type the date directly.",set_today:"Set to today",save_entry:"Save period",save_changes:"Save changes",delete_entry:"Delete this entry",delete_confirm_title:"Delete period entry",delete_confirm_msg:"This entry will be removed, and your average cycle length will be recalculated without it.",cancel:"Cancel",delete:"Delete",invalid_ti